UHD: do not generate a CMake package export in a static build.

Without this, configuring UHD with BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF fails at generate time:

    CMake Error: install(EXPORT "uhdTargets" ...) includes target "uhd" which
    requires target "uhd-resources" that is not in any export set.

and, once uhd-resources is added, the same again for "cmrc-base". Exporting the
uhd target requires every target it links to be in the same export set, and
upstream exports neither the CMakeRC resource library nor its base target. The
failure is specific to static builds; the shared build upstream tests does not
link uhd-resources into the export.

Nothing in this repository consumes UHD through find_package(UHD) -- the browser
side module links libuhd.a directly -- so the package export is simply not
generated. The library, headers and everything else still install normally.

Applied by deps/fetch-deps.sh. Upstream UHD is v4.10.0.0.

--- a/host/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/host/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -620,7 +620,13 @@
 )
 
 include(CMakePackageConfigHelpers)
-if(TARGET uhd)
+# Exporting the uhd target requires every target it links to be in the same
+# export set. In a static build that pulls in uhd-resources (a CMakeRC resource
+# library) and then cmrc-base, neither of which upstream exports, and cmake fails
+# at generate time. Nothing here consumes UHD through find_package(UHD) -- the
+# browser side module links libuhd.a directly -- so the CMake package export is
+# simply not generated.
+if(FALSE)
     export(
         EXPORT uhdTargets
         FILE ${UHD_BINARY_DIR}/cmake/Modules/UHDTargets.cmake
@@ -642,7 +648,7 @@
     DESTINATION ${CMAKE_MODULES_DIR}/uhd
     COMPONENT "devel"
 )
-if(TARGET uhd)
+if(FALSE)  # see the note above: no CMake package export in a static build
     install(
         EXPORT uhdTargets
         FILE UHDTargets.cmake
